# Banking Analytics – Dataset Documentation

## 1. Overview

This project uses synthetic banking data to demonstrate an enterprise-style Credit Risk and Portfolio Intelligence solution developed in Microsoft Power BI.

All records are fictional and created for portfolio demonstration and analytical purposes. No confidential customer or employer data is used.

## 2. Core Datasets

| Dataset | Category | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `Dim_Branch` | Dimension | Branch identifiers, branch names, cities, regions, managers and annual targets |
| `Dim_Customer` | Dimension | Customer identifiers, demographics, age bands, income, employment type and branch mapping |
| `Dim_Product` | Dimension | Loan product categories, base interest rates and maximum tenure |
| `Fact_Loan` | Fact | Loan details, disbursement amounts, outstanding balances, interest rates, loan status and days past due |
| `Fact_Payment` | Fact | Payment schedules, due amounts, paid amounts, payment channels and payment status |
| `Fact_Collections` | Fact | Collection assignments, overdue amounts, recovered amounts, resolution dates and collection status |

## 3. Calculated Tables

The following tables are created inside Power BI using DAX. They are not separate source datasets.

| Calculated Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Dim_Calendar` | Consolidated date dimension based on loan disbursement, collection assignment and payment dates |
| `Portfolio_Performance` | Provides Performing and Non-Performing portfolio categories |
| `Customer_Risk_Segment` | Supports NPA-Exposed and Non-NPA customer segmentation |
| `SecurityAccess` | Stores demonstration user access mappings for Admin, Regional and Branch-level security |

## 4. Key Analytical Areas

- Loan portfolio and outstanding exposure
- NPA and delinquency analysis
- Customer demographics and risk segmentation
- Product and regional portfolio performance
- Branch-level performance and target achievement
- Collections, overdue amounts and recovery performance
- Payment behaviour and collection efficiency

## 5. Data Model

The datasets support a dimensional data model with loan, payment and collection fact tables connected to relevant dimensions.

The model is designed to support interactive reporting, DAX calculations, date-based analysis and branch-level Row-Level Security.

## 6. Data Privacy and Usage

- All banking and customer records are synthetic.
- Names, identifiers, email addresses and financial values are demonstration data.
- Demo security emails are fictional and are not intended for authentication against real banking systems.
- The editable Power BI project file is maintained separately and is not included in this public repository.

## 7. Disclaimer

This project is an independently developed portfolio demonstration. It does not represent an actual bank, financial institution, customer portfolio or production banking system.
